  "narrative": {
    "intro": "BL Harbert International has $971M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 47 awards, with an average award size of $20.6M and obligations up 3.4% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, accounting for $925M of obligations. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the top market, with $921M in obligations, followed by Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction at $45.2M. Recent fiscal-year history shows obligations of $488M in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $1.3B in FY23, $1B in FY24, and $938M in FY25, with FY26 at $971M so far. The Department of State, Department of Justice, NASA, GSA, and DHS are smaller buyers, with obligations of $35.6M, $9.5M, $225K, $220K, and $10K respectively. Architectural Services and Industrial Building Construction appear as additional markets, with $4.3M and $50K in obligations. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity rather than full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
