        "heading": "Who are BL Harbert International's main federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the main buyer, with $925M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of State follows with $35.6M and the Department of Justice with $9.5M. Other buying agencies include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $225K, the General Services Administration at $220K, and the Department of Homeland Security at $10K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services does BL Harbert International sell to the government?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the primary market, with $921M in obligations. Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction accounts for $45.2M, Architectural Services accounts for $4.3M, and Industrial Building Construction accounts for $50K. These markets represent the company’s reported federal contract activity in FY2026 to date."
